    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Royal Ballet Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p>Christopher Wheeldon’s Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland burst onto the stage in 2011 in an explosion of colour, stage magic and inventive, sophisticated choreography. Joby Talbot’s score combines contemporary soundworlds with sweeping melodies that gesture to ballet scores of the 19th century. Bob Crowley’s wildly imaginative, eye-popping designs draw on everything from puppetry to projections to make Wonderland wonderfully real. The result shows The Royal Ballet at its best, bringing together world-class dance with enchanting family entertainment and ingenious music and design. </p>\\n"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@value": "Organization"
      }
